From 4c92a65a099e6a4328ca335cff21127169a2010c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:28:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 07/22] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7125: add A618 GPU OPPs for
 speed-bin 159
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SM7125 (atoll) A618 parts are fused to GPU speed-bin 159, which the
driver maps to opp-supported-hw bit 3. The gpu_opp_table inherited
from sc7180.dtsi has no OPP enabled for that bit, so add the NOM_L1
750 MHz top OPP that this bin tops out at and extend the shared lower
OPPs (180-650 MHz) to it. The TURBO/TURBO_L1 800/825 MHz OPPs stay
sc7180-only.

Override gpu_opp_table from sm7125.dtsi so all SM7125 devices pick up
the change and the sc7180 SKUs are left untouched.

The Galaxy A52 4G (samsung,a52q) then runs at
180/267/355/430/565/650/750 MHz.

Based on the sm7125-mainline tree work by Vitalii Skorkin
<nikroks@mainlining.org>.
Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125.dtsi | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125.dtsi
index a53145a610a3..1cd3f9b27946 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7125.dtsi
@@ -14,3 +14,42 @@
 &cpu5 { compatible = "qcom,kryo465"; };
 &cpu6 { compatible = "qcom,kryo465"; };
 &cpu7 { compatible = "qcom,kryo465"; };
+
+/*
+ * The Adreno 618 on SM7125 (atoll) is fused to GPU speed-bin 159, which the
+ * driver maps to opp-supported-hw bit 3 (0x08). Add the NOM_L1 750 MHz top
+ * OPP this bin tops out at and extend the shared lower OPPs to it. The
+ * TURBO/TURBO_L1 800/825 MHz OPPs stay sc7180-only (no bit 3 set).
+ */
+&gpu_opp_table {
+	opp-750000000 {
+		opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <750000000>;
+		opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
+		opp-peak-kBps = <7216000>;
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x08>;
+	};
+
+	opp-650000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+
+	opp-565000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+
+	opp-430000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+
+	opp-355000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+
+	opp-267000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+
+	opp-180000000 {
+		opp-supported-hw = <0x0f>;
+	};
+};
